NETWORKING

Network cards talk over cables (through relays, too); wireless cards
over the air (tier 1: limited range, tier 2: unlimited and across
dimensions).

  local m = component.modem
  m.open(123)
  m.send(address, 123, "hello", 42)
  m.broadcast(123, "anyone?")
  local _, _, from, port, distance, a, b = event.pull("modem_message")

The net library adds hostnames: net.discover(), net.resolve(name),
net.send, net.broadcast, net.receive(timeout, port). Programs:
ping, msg, hostname.

Cables also connect computers to screens, keyboards, disk drives,
adapters and redstone I/O blocks; they appear in component.list().
Relays pass messages but not components.

Wireless peripherals: use the Linker. Right-click a computer or rack,
then right-click blocks to link them. With a wireless card the
computer sees linked screens, drives and inventories as components.
